  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We have two pairs of vertical angles, and we know that vertical angles are congruent and therefore have the same measure. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠1 & =m∠2, \\\\ m∠3 & =m∠4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are told that $m∠1={35}^{∘}$ and $m∠4={111}^{∘},$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{35}^{∘} & =m∠2, \\\\ m∠3 & ={111}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠2+m∠3 & ={35}^{∘}+{111}^{∘} \\\\  & ={146}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
